    "Downloads: the cached base snapshot held only model.safetensors, so its config and tokenizer files were downloaded at the same revision (11.5 MB); not in the plan's estimate.",
    "Attempt 1 failed: run.sh started 2026-11-03T04:29:54Z and the runner stopped its training at 04:40:32Z, after step 140 (the last logged step), because the MPS allocator kept cached buffers of every new batch shape: the process footprint reached 42 GB (41 GB IOAccelerator), system swap reached 28 GB, and steps slowed from about 0.7 s to 15-27 s from step 111 on. Fix: train.py calls torch.mps.empty_cache() after every optimizer step and logs what the allocator held before the release. Attempt 1's partial training log (140 steps) and its incomplete receipt are kept in results/attempt1/ (its adapters and run log in raw/attempt1/, gitignored). A 60-step check started right after attempt 1, while the system was still swapping, ran slowly and was stopped; a 12-step check then ran at 0.65 to 1.13 s per step with 8.1 to 13.3 GiB held, and its printed losses (four decimals) equalled attempt 1's for all 12 steps. The run was restarted from scratch (attempt 2, this receipt)."
